b02eb9cBe142417b" target=3D"_blank" style=3D"text-decoration: underline; co=
lor: #006699;" rel=3D"noopener">Katy Balls explains all</a>. Meanwhile, as =
speculation about fresh attacks on Iran grows, Mark Urban analyses <a href=
=3D"https://link.thetimes.com/click/48317404.442289/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cudGhldGl=
tZXMuY29tL3dvcmxkL21pZGRsZS1lYXN0L2FydGljbGUvdGVuc2lvbnMtdXMtaXJhbi1pc3JhZW=
wtbDVrMmw5ZG1k/6a464fcf7d55e1fcfb02eb9cB853fb482" target=3D"_blank" style=
=3D"text-decoration: underline; color: #006699;" rel=3D"noopener">the state=
 of the Tehran regime</a>, its faltering economy and its military preparedn=
ess.</span>
</p><p style=3D"margin:0;font-size:18px;mso-line-height-alt:21px">&nbsp;</p=
><p style=3D"margin:0;font-size:18px;mso-line-height-alt:27px">
<span style=3D"word-break: break-word; font-size: 18px;">In August we lost =
our wonderful columnist Rod Liddle who passed away at the age of 66. Rod le=
ft three children and today his eldest, Wilder, writes about&nbsp;<a href=
